Ghidra oversized THREE of them: 2ce4 undefined4 (a 4-byte store spans 0x6ce4..0x6ce7 -> zeroes 2ce6 AND
2ce7), 2ce6 undefined2 (a 2-byte store spans 0x6ce6..0x6ce7 -> zeroes 2ce7), 2ce7 undefined2 (a 2-byte
READ spans 0x6ce7..0x6ce8 -> the test picks up the 2ce8 counter's low byte).  In FUN_0000_4886, both
`DAT_2000_2ce6 = 2` (word store) and `DAT_2000_2ce4 = 0x5db8` (dword store) therefore clobber the
enter-cockpit flag 2ce7 the cascade just set.  Retyping 2ce4->undefined2, 2ce6->undefined1,
2ce7->undefined1 makes every store/read exactly the asm width: no cross-clobber, and 2ce7's test reads
only its own byte.  2ce4 as a WORD near-code-offset is still dispatched identically (`(*2ce4)()` reads the
same low 16 bits 0xc30e/0x773e).

